PROJECT REPORT STRUCTURE

1. Title Page
- Project title
- Institution name
- Department
- Team members
- Guide/supervisor
- Academic year

2. Certificate
- Completion and approval statement

3. Acknowledgement
- Thanks to guide, institution, contributors

4. Abstract
- Problem overview
- Proposed solution
- Technologies used
- Key outcomes

5. Table of Contents
- Chapters and section page numbers

6. List of Figures and Tables
- ER diagram, DFD, architecture, screenshots, test tables

7. Introduction
7.1 Background
7.2 Motivation
7.3 Objectives
7.4 Scope of project
7.5 Document organization

8. Problem Statement
8.1 Existing system limitations
8.2 Need for automation
8.3 Functional goals and constraints

9. Literature Survey
9.1 Related attendance systems
9.2 Face recognition approaches
9.3 Comparison of methods/tools
9.4 Gap analysis

10. Proposed Methodology
10.1 Overall approach
10.2 Data flow from camera to dashboard
10.3 Face detection and recognition workflow
10.4 Attendance marking logic
10.5 Security and authentication approach

11. System Architecture and Design
11.1 High-level architecture
11.2 Module decomposition
11.3 ER diagram explanation
11.4 DFD level 0 and level 1 explanation
11.5 API design summary

12. Implementation Details
12.1 Backend implementation (Spring Boot)
12.2 AI service implementation (Python)
12.3 Frontend implementation (React + TypeScript)
12.4 Database schema and seed data
12.5 Docker and deployment setup

13. User Interface and Screenshots
13.1 Login page
13.2 Dashboard
13.3 Students page
13.4 Attendance page
13.5 Admin/teacher workflows

14. Testing and Validation
14.1 Testing strategy
14.2 Unit test cases
14.3 Integration test cases
14.4 User acceptance test cases
14.5 Defects and fixes
14.6 Result summary

15. Results and Discussion
15.1 Functional outcomes
15.2 Performance observations
15.3 Accuracy and practical limitations

16. Conclusion
- Summary of achievements
- Practical impact

17. Future Scope
- Liveness detection
- Multi-camera support
- Notifications and analytics
- Timetable and ERP integration

18. References
- Books, papers, docs, websites

19. Appendices
- API sample payloads
- Config files
- Deployment scripts
- Additional test logs
